Release notes for the modern-linux fork of OOC (oo2c)
=====================================================

Bug reports: https://github.com/tkurtbond/oo2c/issues

oo2c 2.2.1
----------

Fixes the build on Debian and Ubuntu.  Tested on Fedora 44 and 45 with
gcc 16, and on Ubuntu 26.04 with gcc 15.

* Programs are linked with the libraries of the run-time system (-lm,
  -lgc, ...) even when liboo2c is a shared library.  Generated C calls
  libm directly, and on Debian and Ubuntu, whose libtool and linker do
  not pass on a shared library's dependencies, the 2.2.0 tarball
  failed to link bin/oo2c ("DSO missing from command line").
* CI on GitHub: build, self-host and test on current Fedora and Ubuntu
  (.github/ci-build.sh).

oo2c 2.2.0
----------

The first release of this fork, based on OOC 2.1.11 (the last upstream
release; development stopped around 2011).  It builds and runs on
current Linux: tested on Fedora 44 with gcc 16, glibc 2.4x, Boehm gc
8.2, libtool 2.5 and autoconf 2.72.  The release tarball
oo2c_64-2.2.0.tar.bz2 bootstraps on a 64-bit system with no oo2c
installed.

Language and compiler changes:

* Using a local (nested) procedure as a procedure value is now an
  error (error 81), as the Oberon-2 report requires.  The generated C
  would have needed an executable stack.  Programs that did this and
  compiled with 2.1.11 must be changed.
* Array types with a negative length are rejected.
* A type guard is allowed on the target of an assignment.
* ARRAY OF BYTE parameters get the byte size of an open array
  argument, not its element count.
* The optimizer folds comparisons of a non-real value with itself
  (x=x, x<x, ...).

Generated C and build:

* Generated C compiles with gcc 16 without warnings: program main
  files declare OOC_<Module>_open, libc functions taking char* are
  called through C wrappers, and every generated file silences gcc's
  -Wunused-label, -Wunused-but-set-variable and -Wunused-parameter.
* configure adds -fno-strict-aliasing for gcc, which applies to every
  program oo2c compiles.
* libtool is called with --tag=CC instead of --tag=CXX, so -lm is not
  dropped from liboo2c.la with libtool 2.x.
* With --enable-threads=pthreads, GC_THREADS is defined for Boehm gc 7
  and later, so thread stacks are scanned.
* configure.ac and aclocal.m4 are updated for autoconf 2.72.
* Runtime C files and hand-written library C are fixed for -Wall
  -Wextra and deprecated APIs.
* `make dist` works again and names the tarball after the pointer size
  (oo2c_32 or oo2c_64).

Tests:

* The 64-bit reference C output of tests/ssa-c-output is in git, stale
  test data is fixed, and the hostess test cases run with the v2 test
  framework (make test-hostess-ooc1).

The shared library is still liboo2c.so.3.
